Subject: [PATCH] plasmaquick/configview: use the applet's own icon for the
 config dialog window

ConfigView hardcodes the window icon to the generic theme icon
"configure", so every widget's configuration dialog shows the same gear
in the task switcher/taskbar instead of the widget's own icon.

Use the applet's metadata icon name when one is set, falling back to
"configure" otherwise.

Why FrameWidge cares: a pure-QML plasmoid cannot override this itself -
QWindow::icon is not a Q_PROPERTY and setIcon() is neither a slot nor
Q_INVOKABLE, so the configDialog context property exposed to the
applet's KCM pages cannot change the window icon from QML. Verified
against Qt 6.11: no meta-object entry "icon" on QQuickWindow, and no
registered QString/QUrl/QPixmap/QImage -> QIcon converters.

Applies to: plasma-framework master, src/plasmaquick/configview.cpp

--- a/src/plasmaquick/configview.cpp
+++ b/src/plasmaquick/configview.cpp
@@ -ConfigView::ConfigView(Plasma::Applet *applet, QWindow *parent)
     : QQuickWindow(parent)
     , d(new ConfigViewPrivate(applet, this))
 {
-    setIcon(QIcon::fromTheme(QStringLiteral("configure")));
+    const QString appletIcon = applet->pluginMetaData().iconName();
+    setIcon(QIcon::fromTheme(appletIcon.isEmpty() ? QStringLiteral("configure") : appletIcon));
     // Only register types once
     [[maybe_unused]] static int configModelRegisterResult = qmlRegisterType<ConfigModel>("org.kde.plasma.configuration", 2, 0, "ConfigModel");
     [[maybe_unused]] static int configCategoryRegisterResult = qmlRegisterType<ConfigCategory>("org.kde.plasma.configuration", 2, 0, "ConfigCategory");
     d->init();
